    description: "WHAT. framework_patterns._apply_subresource_locator_paths keys classes by short name across every file and language: class_by_name is last write wins, methods_by_class merges the methods of every class that shares a name, and propagated_prefixes is keyed by the return type's short name. Two resource classes named alike in two packages are one class to it.\n\nWHY IT WAS LEFT. PR #2326 gave the other two name tables of this file the reference_candidates rule (host language, qualified name before name, source order). This table needs a different candidate set: a Kotlin locator can return a Java resource class, so the JVM languages are one set, and the return type should be resolved through the locator file's imports, not by short name. Since PR #2326 the symbol list order is fixed, so the table's answer is the same in every run; it is still not chosen by anything the source says.\n\nASK. Resolve a locator's return type to one class (imports, then package), key the propagation by class id, and stop merging namesakes' methods.\n\nNOT CHECKED. Whether any corpus repository has two JAX-RS resource classes of one short name.\n\nFound during PR #2326 (2026-11-22)."  # fd24
